interface curvature at the particle nose is required to model interfacial mass, momentum and
heat transfers.

As shown in Fig. 1, drop shapes in viscous and surface tension force dominant regimes
can be represented by using two parameters, the aspect ratio *E* and the distortion factor γ,
which are defined by

$$
E=\frac{b_{1}+b_{2}}{2a}
$$

(4)

$$
\gamma=\frac{2b_{2}}{b_{1}+b_{2}}
$$

(5)

where *a* isahalfofthemajoraxis,*b₁* and *b₂* are the distances from the major axis to the
bottom and the top of a drop, respectively.

