Since all the single drops in the present experiments rose rectilinearly without any shape
oscillation and had axisymmetric shapes, sphere-volume equivalent diameters *d*, distortion
factors γ and aspect ratios *E* were measured from images recorded by the single high-speed
video camera. Images were taken at 400 mm above the nozzle tip, at which all drops reached
terminal conditions. Spatial resolution of images ranged from 0.02 to 0.18 mm/pixel. Measurement uncertainties estimated at 95% confidence were 2.0, 3.0, 2.0, 0.81, 1.0 and 0.6% for
ρ, µ, σ, *d*, *E* and γ, respectively. The details of experiments can be found in the previous
paper<sup>(13)</sup>.

